Track copies into the daemon store as downloads/uploads.

Nix reports the store of a daemon-connected client as `daemon`, so e.g.
`nix copy --from ssh-ng://...` (and any `nix build` run through the
daemon) logs

  copying path '/nix/store/...' from 'ssh-ng://...' to 'daemon'

i.e. a CopyPath activity whose destination parses to `Host _ _ "daemon"`.
`parseHost` only recognised "", local, local://, unix and unix:// as
`Localhost`, so none of the `CopyPath ... Localhost` cases in `NOM.Update`
matched: the transfer was never entered into runningDownloads (nor
runningUploads for `nix copy --to`), its Progress results went nowhere,
and nom showed the copy as a bare line with no progress bar.

Treat `daemon` as `Localhost`. Display is unaffected (a Localhost peer
renders as no host label) and the `Build ... on <host>` matching is
untouched: builder hostnames never parse to this.

diff --git a/nix-output-monitor/lib/NOM/Builds.hs b/nix-output-monitor/lib/NOM/Builds.hs
--- a/nix-output-monitor/lib/NOM/Builds.hs
+++ b/nix-output-monitor/lib/NOM/Builds.hs
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ parseIndentedStoreObject = either fail pure . TextParser.parseOnly indentedStor
 
 parseHost :: Text -> Host WithContext
 parseHost hostname
-  | hostname `elem` ["", "local", "local://", "unix", "unix://"] = Localhost
+  | hostname `elem` ["", "local", "local://", "unix", "unix://", "daemon"] = Localhost
   | otherwise = Host proto user host
  where
   (proto, (user, host)) = second (breakOnMaybe "@") $ breakOnMaybe "://" hostname
